<title>ITALY: Enel -led group wins UK power plant order.</title>
<headline>Enel -led group wins UK power plant order.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A consortium of Italian companies formed by electricity utility Enel, Ansaldo, Fiat's FiatAvio and the Federici group's Sicel has won an order from Yorkshire Electricity Group Plc's Yorkshire Cogeneration Ltd to supply a 50 megawatt combined cycle power plant at Thornhill in Yorkshire.</p>
<p>An Enel statement gave no financial details.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
